Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20Fiber=20places=20fiber=20objects=20only?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20CE/CTO/splitter/ODF/pigtail/slack?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Applies the module-separation rule to the Fiber map. Fiber stops
creating civil structures and cameras; those belong to Ductería and
CCTV.

- src/lib/fiberNodeTypes.ts (new): the fiber placement catalog —
  Splice Closure (CE), Terminal Box (CTO), Splitter, ODF/DIO, Pigtail,
  Fiber Slack, Existing Fiber Source — with tag prefixes (CE-001,
  CTO-001, ...) and, for the objects that hold splices, the enclosure
  they auto-create. Also the helpers that mark a node as owned by
  another module.
- migration: fiber_nodes.node_type and fiber_enclosures.enclosure_type
  check constraints extended with the fiber types. The civil and camera
  values stay valid so the ~173 existing rows keep working — this is a
  menu change, not a data migration.
- createFiberNode: a CE/CTO/splitter/ODF now creates its
  fiber_enclosures row too, so a closure dropped on the map is
  immediately usable in the splice/fusion views instead of being an
  empty marker. The conduit_structures mirror is untouched and simply
  never fires for the new types.
- FiberMapCanvas: placement menu driven by the catalog, with map icons
  per fiber object (closure seam, CTO drop ports, splitter triangle,
  ODF rack, pigtail, coiled slack). Ductería/CCTV nodes are hidden by
  default behind a new "Show Context" toggle; when shown they are
  dimmed, non-draggable and non-clickable.
- FiberConnectivityDiagram: nodes owned by other modules only appear
  when they actually carry fiber (a cable lands on them or they hold an
  enclosure) — this alone drops ~39 unconnected cameras that were
  padding the diagram.

Not included: BOM lines for the new fiber objects. That needs real part
numbers and costs from the hardware catalog rather than invented ones.

